Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: https://github.com/airockchip/rknn-llm
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Suggests: cmake, g++, pkg-config, libopencv-dev, python3-flask
Description: Rockchip RKLLM runtime for NPU platforms (RK3588/RK3576/RK3562/RV1126B)
 This package ships the Rockchip RKLLM software stack for deploying large
 language models on Rockchip NPU devices. It contains the shared runtime
 library librkllmrt.so, the public C/C++ header, CMake and pkg-config
 integration files, board tuning scripts and the upstream example sources.
 .
 It also installs /usr/bin/rkllm, a command line front end written against the
 Python standard library only. It needs no compilation and no pip packages and
 drives the runtime directly through ctypes:
   rkllm chat <model>     interactive local chat
   rkllm run  <model> ..  one-shot inference
   rkllm serve <model>    OpenAI-compatible HTTP API (optionally via the
                          shipped rkllm-server.service)
   rkllm list / rkllm info / rkllm selftest
 .
 Models are not included: compile them from HuggingFace checkpoints with the
 RKLLM toolkit on an x86 host first. The runtime needs the rknpu kernel driver
 that your board image provides; this package never ships or builds it.
 .
 Documentation PDFs are installed under /usr/share/doc/@PACKAGE@/ and the
 example sources under /usr/share/@PACKAGE@/examples/.
